═══ qualify ═══
putnami qualify

Derive the smoke contract from the workload's route inventory, execute it against --target (local composes the workload with compose; a URL is any deployed environment), and print one verdict bound to the tested tree or to the deployed sha. Fails closed: unsupported, not_run, timed_out, canceled, target_unreachable, digest_mismatch and composition_failed are distinct from passed and exit non-zero

Usage:
  putnami qualify <project> --target <local|url> [--expect-sha <sha>] [--platform-prefix <path>] [--ready-timeout <duration>] [--request-timeout <duration>] [--print-contract] [--output <format>]

Command Flags:
  --target <local|url>         local composes the workload on this machine; an http(s) URL is a running deployment
  --expect-sha <sha>           Required with a URL target: the git sha the deployment must report on /version
  --platform-prefix <path>     Prefix under which /readyz and /version are mounted; setting it makes local readiness poll <path>/readyz instead of waiting for the startup claim; default: where the route inventory declares both, else the root
  --ready-timeout <duration>   Deadline for readiness; default 60s
  --request-timeout <duration> Deadline per smoke request; default 5s
  --print-contract             Print the derived contract and exit without a target

Examples:
  putnami qualify /go/samples/migrations-feature --target local
  putnami qualify @example/06-database --target https://pr-123.preview.example --expect-sha 3cc91b658
  putnami qualify /go/samples/migrations-feature --print-contract --output=json

Global Options:
  Common: --verbose, --debug, --watch, --plan, --help
  Project Selection: --all, --impacted, --projects, --tag, --exclude-tag, --exclude, --baseline, --impacted-strict
  Execution: --where, --providers, --credential-fd, --no-cache, --no-cache-projects, --cache-trust, --continue-on-error, --max-parallel, --resource, --cpu-policy, --retry, --retry-failed, --profile, --dry-run
  Output: --output, --json, --quiet, --color, --no-color
  Advanced: --trace-profile

