═══ sessions inspect ═══
putnami sessions inspect

Show full details and event stream for a specific session. --run names a remote attempt instead of a session: the attempt reference or submission key printed when a --where remote run was submitted, resolved through the durable attempt records under .putnami/runner/attempts. An attempt whose session is already imported is shown from the local store; one that is not (the CLI died mid-run, the import failed) is resumed through the workspace's runner provider from the persisted cursor and imported through the same path, and nothing is ever resubmitted. Ctrl-C during a resumed follow cancels the attempt within bounded time

Usage:
  putnami sessions inspect [<id>] [--run <ref>] [--output <format>]

Command Flags:
  --run <ref>                  Inspect the session of a remote attempt by its attempt reference or submission key, resuming the attempt first when it was never imported

Examples:
  putnami sessions inspect abc123
  putnami sessions inspect latest
  putnami sessions inspect --run fixture-attempt-42

Global Options:
  Common: --verbose, --debug, --watch, --plan, --help
  Project Selection: --all, --impacted, --projects, --tag, --exclude-tag, --exclude, --baseline, --impacted-strict
  Execution: --where, --providers, --credential-fd, --no-cache, --no-cache-projects, --cache-trust, --continue-on-error, --max-parallel, --resource, --cpu-policy, --retry, --retry-failed, --profile, --dry-run
  Output: --output, --json, --quiet, --color, --no-color
  Advanced: --trace-profile

Related Commands:
  putnami sessions list

═══ sessions list ═══
putnami sessions list

Show recent execution sessions with timing and status. --revision keeps the sessions whose recorded tree sat on the named commit (a lowercase hex prefix of its id, 7 to 64 characters) and adds the head commit and the actual placement to each row, so a new session can find what judged a given revision; a session that recorded no tree never matches. --output=jsonl rows carry revision and placement when the record states them

Usage:
  putnami sessions list [--revision <sha>] [--output <format>]

Command Flags:
  --revision <sha>             Keep only sessions whose recorded tree sat on this commit; a lowercase hex prefix of the commit id, never a ref name

Examples:
  putnami sessions list
  putnami sessions list --revision 7194fc3537
  putnami sessions list --output=jsonl

Global Options:
  Common: --verbose, --debug, --watch, --plan, --help
  Project Selection: --all, --impacted, --projects, --tag, --exclude-tag, --exclude, --baseline, --impacted-strict
  Execution: --where, --providers, --credential-fd, --no-cache, --no-cache-projects, --cache-trust, --continue-on-error, --max-parallel, --resource, --cpu-policy, --retry, --retry-failed, --profile, --dry-run
  Output: --output, --json, --quiet, --color, --no-color
  Advanced: --trace-profile

Related Commands:
  putnami sessions inspect

═══ sessions replay ═══
putnami sessions replay

Replay retained session artifacts through each explicitly selected reporter extension (session-reporter, log-reporter) that has not delivered them. Each resumes from its own acknowledgement cursor with fresh reporter credentials, without running graph work. Incomplete delivery returns an error and keeps the bounded checkpoint for another replay

Usage:
  putnami sessions replay --session <id>

Command Flags:
  --session <id>               Exact retained session id; latest is not accepted

Examples:
  putnami sessions replay --session 20260914-120000-abc123

Global Options:
  Common: --verbose, --debug, --watch, --plan, --help
  Project Selection: --all, --impacted, --projects, --tag, --exclude-tag, --exclude, --baseline, --impacted-strict
  Execution: --where, --providers, --credential-fd, --no-cache, --no-cache-projects, --cache-trust, --continue-on-error, --max-parallel, --resource, --cpu-policy, --retry, --retry-failed, --profile, --dry-run
  Output: --output, --json, --quiet, --color, --no-color
  Advanced: --trace-profile

