═══ workspace init ═══
putnami workspace init

Initialize a new workspace

Usage:
  putnami init [--workspace <name>] [--extension <ts|go|py>] [--project <name>] [--project-path <path>] [--channel <channel>] [--force]

Command Flags:
  --workspace <name>           Workspace name override
  --extension <ts|go|py>       Default extension to install
  --project <name>             Create an initial project
  --project-path <path>        Workspace-relative path for the initial project
  --channel <channel>          Resolve the extensions, the template and the starter dependencies on one release channel (default: PUTNAMI_CHANNEL, then the channel the CLI was installed from, then latest)
  --force                      Reinitialize an existing workspace

Examples:
  putnami init
  putnami init --project my-app
  putnami init --project my-app --project-path apps/my-app
  putnami init --project my-app --channel canary

Global Options:
  Common: --verbose, --debug, --watch, --plan, --help
  Project Selection: --all, --impacted, --projects, --tag, --exclude-tag, --exclude, --baseline, --impacted-strict
  Execution: --where, --providers, --credential-fd, --no-cache, --no-cache-projects, --cache-trust, --continue-on-error, --max-parallel, --resource, --cpu-policy, --retry, --retry-failed, --profile, --dry-run
  Output: --output, --json, --quiet, --color, --no-color
  Advanced: --trace-profile

